  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1-{csch}^{4}⁡x}{{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,{coth}^{2}⁡x-{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the cotangent-cosecant identity \n\n$$\n{csc}^{2}⁡x-1={cot}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, we get the hyperbolic identity\n\n$$\n1+{csch}^{2}⁡x={coth}^{2}⁡x.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we rewrite the integral and evaluate it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1-{csch}^{4}⁡x}{{csch}^{2}⁡x\\,{coth}^{2}⁡x-{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{(1+{csch}^{2}⁡x)(1-{csch}^{2}⁡x)}{-{coth}^{2}⁡x(1-{csch}^{2}⁡x)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1+{csch}^{2}⁡x}{-{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{{coth}^{2}⁡x}{-{coth}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =-(4-2) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
